 "id": "ttl/mixed-1h-head-5m-tail/read-after-10-minutes",
 "description": "r0 sends a 1h mark on messages[1] and a 5m mark on messages[2]. The change shrinks messages[1] from 3,000 to 1,000 tokens. The forwarded head is 2,000 + 1,000 = 3,000 tokens (1h), the tail 2,000 (5m): r0 writes 5,000, of which 3,000 at 1h. r1 comes 10 minutes later with marks on messages[1] (1h) and messages[3] (5m). The provider reads the 3,000-token 1h head and writes the 2,000 tail and the 500 new message again: read 3,000, write 2,500. The 5m tail expired, the 1h head did not. The host reports Facts.TTL 5m. The replayed 2,000 tokens are inside the head, so they are READ (2,000 x $0.30/M), not written. Before the fix the phase was cold and the saving a 1h write (2,000 x $6.00/M).",
